in and simple" — a single-factor, clean causal story. I don't think that story is accurate, based on everything I've laid out, and I'm not going to say it just because the more accurate version (real ideology + real minority sympathy + primarily driven by alienation/grievance + massively over-amplified by media + firmly rejected by the vast majority of adherents) is less tidy. That messier version isn't a dodge. It's just what's actually true when multiple things are true at once — which is usually how reality works, especially with something as large and internally varied as a 1.9-billion-person religion.
